{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/14953-ephemeral-lineages","id":14953,"title":"Ephemeral Lineages","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-20T16:31:13-08:00","id":14953,"title":"Ephemeral Lineages","content":"The new World of Darkness has always drawn a distinction between spirits and ghosts; but <b>God-Machine Chronicle</b> has taken it up a notch by declaring that spirits and ghosts are made of different kinds of ephemera, and then adding a third kind of ephemeral being (angels) that are made of their own kind of ephemera.<br /> <br /> This, I think, is the genius behind Benjamin Beard\u2019s <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/14531-the-samedi-a-replacement-lineage-for-the-ulgan\">Samedi </a>and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/3999-god-machine-lineage\">Seraphim </a>Lineages: instead of going for a core of five Lineages (with Ulgans feeling like something of a fifth wheel), he appears to be going with a set of four \u201celemental Lineages\u201d (the Fire-based Frankensteins, the Air-based Galeteids, the Water-based Osirans, and the Earth-based Tammuz) and a separate set of \u201cephemeral Lineages\u201d (including the spirit-based Ulgans, the ghost-based Samedi, and the angel-based Seraphim). My initial reaction to that last one was \u201cwhy?\u201d \u2014 but given this context, I can definitely get behind the idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 11-20-2013, 07:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-20T23:05:02-08:00","id":15164,"title":"","content":"This was absolutely unintended but if it makes some kind of thematic sense or ties them together nicely in your mind I am more than happy to endorse it!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/806-benjamin-beard","name":"Benjamin Beard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar806_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T09:35:47-08:00","id":15437,"title":"","content":"I think you could come up with four spirit lineages, that also partake of the elements: the earth-based Ulgans, dealing with spirits of the world around us; the water-based Samedi, rooted in the deep echoes of memory and grief and ghosts; the fire-based Seraphim, rooted in angels patterned after invention and transformation; and perhaps my own Delphi idea, air-based, and rooted in the whispers of secrets and oracular visions. Fire's the weak link there, though fire is one of our first technologies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T12:22:12-08:00","id":15519,"title":"","content":"Fire is an excellent association for the angel-oriented ephemeral Lineage \u2014 after all, we\u2019re talking about the gameline where everything is oriented around stories like Prometheus stealing fire from the gods in order to teach man how to survive on his own. As for Air, I\u2019ll just note that astral entities also qualify as ephemeral beings, of a type distinct from spirits, ghosts, and angels.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T12:49:39-08:00","id":15543,"title":"","content":"Too bad the Hedge beings aren't ephemeral, they would make a good fit for Air.<br /> <br /> Demons (Inferno style) are ephemeral, but I don't know how well those would line up with the element of Air. Maybe in that &quot;hot wind&quot; and Djinn kind of way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-09T21:25:55-08:00","id":26980,"title":"","content":"Thinking up elemental associations for the ephemeral Lineages is fun; but really, I wouldn\u2019t want to try to shoehorn them into the four-elements model. It\u2019s more important that each Lineage be reflective of the type of ephemera that it\u2019s tied to; and the list of ephemeral bengs s likely to grow. As is, we have:<br /> <br /> \u2022 from <b>Vampire: the Requiem</b>, the Strix are kinda-sorta ephemeral beings, though not really. I wouldn\u2019t bother with a Lineage for them.<br /> \u2022 <b>Werewolf: the Forsaken</b> gives us spirits. The resulting Ulgan Lineage really needs to reflect the animism on which the spirit world is based.<br /> \u2022 <b>Mage: the Awakening</b> features a number of options, though the one that\u2019s unique to the game is the Astral entities. Note that <b>Magnum Opus</b> has a Dream-born Lineage.<br /> \u2022 <b>Promethean: the Created</b> has the <i>qashmallim</i>. However, they\u2019re too closely related to Prometheans, and too reminiscent of the GM\u2019s angels, to get their own Lineage IMHO.<br /> \u2022 <b>Changeling: the Lost</b> has nothing. I wouldn\u2019t mind adding Will-o-Wisps to the Hedge; but that would be a fan-splat in its own right, and I try not to do fan-splats based off of other fan-splats.<br /> \u2022 <b>Hunter: the Vigil</b> has everything and nothing.<br /> \u2022 <b>Geist: the Sin-Eaters</b> has ghosts, geists, Kerberoi, and other denizens of the Underworld.<br /> \u2022 <b>Mummy: the Curse</b> has a class of Lifeless who reside in Twilight. I\u2019m debating if they\u2019d qualify as ghost-like entities, or if the unique nature of the <b>Mummy</b> metaphysics would classify them as a separate type of ephemera. For now, I\u2019m classifying them as ghost-like.<br /> \u2022 <b>Demon: the Descent</b> has the God-Machine\u2019s angels.<br /> \u2022 And finally, there are the demons of <b>World of Darkness: Inferno</b>. Some have merged with ghosts and spirits (<i>qashmallim</i> are explicitly prohibited, and I suspect that the GM\u2019s angels are likewise), while others are \u201ctrue\u201d demons, neither ghost nor spirt nor anything else but themselves.<br /> <br /> So we\u2019ve got spirits, astral entities, ghosts, angels, and demons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 12-10-2013, 04:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-09T21:58:15-08:00","id":26992,"title":"","content":"A Lineage based on the Qasmallim would defeat the purpose of the Qashmallim.<br /> Ghosts would definitely be welcome, though I am in the &quot;Osirians interact with the dead&quot; camp.<br /> I'm still unsure what's wrong with the Ulgan. I like them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S8EuNtxeJKwq4sKVVPe16_N0ylIashKpgfCCuA1UOM8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Promethean Homebrew.</a><br /> <br /> Yes, I made it the same way as a Promethean. No, the authorities haven't found me yet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","name":"Ben Quo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar685_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-09T22:48:38-08:00","id":27012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ben Quo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/14953-ephemeral-lineages?p=26992#post26992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Lineage based on the Qasmallim would defeat the purpose of the Qashmallim.<br /> Ghosts would definitely be welcome, though I am in the &quot;Osirians interact with the dead&quot; camp.<br /> I'm still unsure what's wrong with the Ulgan. I like them.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm likewise leery of models that look this arbitrary; it's a large part of why I discounted the Prodigal Demiurge section of Magnum Opus for so long.<br /> <br /> Also, Data, you've gone and interposed some of the cWoD gamelines there. May wanna fix.<br /> <br /> Re: Will-O-Wisps: Autumn Nightmares, p137.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 12-10-2013, 01:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T01:33:02-08:00","id":27061,"title":"","content":"Fixed. And thanks for the Will-o-Wisps catch. <br /> <br /> On the subject of the Ulgans, I like them too, for the most part; it\u2019s just that they\u2019ve always felt like a fifth wheel to me. Because, well, they <i>are</i> a fifth wheel: the alchemical theories that serve as the basis for the other four Lineages don\u2019t make allowance for an \u201cEctoplasmic Humour\u201d. <br /> <br /> But if the Ulgans are part of their very own set of Lineages, ones that are defined specifically by being based off of ephemeral substances (spirit stuff, ghostly plasm, whatever it is that angels are made of, whatever the Inferno\u2019s demons are made of, the \u201cdreamstuff\u201d that Astral entities are made of, etc.), then they\u2019re not a fifth wheel anymore. The rest is about giving appropriately thematic flavor to each otherworldly substance, using the various ephemeral beings as an organizing principle. Their inclusion with the original Lineages was arbitrary; this feels more natural to me, and gives them their own place.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T03:57:47-08:00","id":27107,"title":"","content":"I would say amkhata are their own category. Mummy really goes balls to the wall with their dealings with ghosts, via a variety of affinities, utterances, and relics, and that seems to imply a pretty clear distinction versus amkhata.<br /> <br /> If one wanted to say amkhata were more similar to ghosts or to spirits or to whatever then that would make for an interesting story, but my default assumption is that they're their own thing.<br /> <br /> Chthonians, on the other hand...Mummy utterances are pretty wild, hm?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T08:19:03-08:00","id":27204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/14953-ephemeral-lineages?p=27061#post27061\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the subject of the Ulgans, I like them too, for the most part; it\u2019s just that they\u2019ve always felt like a fifth wheel to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aether/quintessence has been a part of alchemical lore since medieval times.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Because, well, they are a fifth wheel: the alchemical theories that serve as the basis for the other four Lineages don\u2019t make allowance for an \u201cEctoplasmic Humour\u201d. </div> </div> </div>&quot;The body must still be that of one who had an affinity for spirits: the descendent of shamans, someone with red hair and the Second Sight, one born with the signs of witch-folk or someone who was particularly devout. Those who have experienced interaction with spirits are also likely candidates.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;It was noted that there was very little presence of quintessence within the terrestrial sphere. Due to the low presence of quintessence, earth could be affected by what takes place within the heavenly bodies.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;That which is Below corresponds to that which is Above, and that which is Above corresponds to that which is Below, to accomplish the miracle of the One Thing.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Lineage that is elementally infused with the stuff that binds the cosmos together has an affinity for spotting connections that might otherwise be overlooked and is made with the bodies of people who have ties with the supernatural elements of the world that are connected to earthly affairs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But if the Ulgans are part of their very own set of Lineages, ones that are defined specifically by being based off of ephemeral substances (spirit stuff, ghostly plasm, whatever it is that angels are made of, whatever the Inferno\u2019s demons are made of, the \u201cdreamstuff\u201d that Astral entities are made of, etc.), then they\u2019re not a fifth wheel anymore. </div> </div> </div>Right. They're instead sequestered off in their own arbitrary category like the Hazmat Lineages were.<br /> <br /> I didn't especially like the Hazmat Lineages. They felt shallow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 12-10-2013, 11:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T10:52:57-08:00","id":27311,"title":"","content":"For what it's worth, they never felt like a fifth wheel to me. They felt like outsiders, which is excellent - they are outsiders. Nobody but nobody knows the things they know or sees the shit they see. They are from stage one exposed to things that drive normal men crazy and make other Prometheans say &quot;Bro, you're loose a screw.&quot;<br /> So if they feel like outsiders then I think that's probably exquisite design. Their Humour is a bit strange - and the book even calls them out on it, saying it's black where ectoplasm, traditionally, is white - and they interact with Spirits, but that means they see the world as no one can (or was <i>meant to</i>).<br /> <br /> The difference between a fifth wheel and an outsider, in this context, is that the &quot;Fifth Wheel&quot; is just along for funsies. They exist only by way of perceived &quot;necessity&quot; to the group, or they're the group's butt-monkey. They are shoe-horned in. The Riven, though, don't feel shoe-horned in to me; they feel fucked-up and strange and like they have brushed the alien, <i>because they have,</i> and that makes them scary. Arbitrary structure around &quot;Ephemeral Lineages&quot; (or replacing them with another ghost-based Lineage, cough-cough) would certainly make them seem like a fifth wheel.<br /> Conversely, &quot;the outsider&quot; is that guy or gal who is very clearly not like everyone else, but is still present. Carrie (from &quot;Carrie&quot;) is an outsider. So is &quot;May&quot; (from &quot;May&quot;). H.P. Lovecraft's &quot;The Outsider&quot; does an exquisite job of being at once existentially terrifying and embodying what I'm talking about here. The Ulgan aren't an afterthought; they're freaking coming in from without and that's scary. They have a vantage point others don't; the fifth wheel, though, doesn't have any vantage point.<br /> He's in the trunk of the car while the other four have fun.<br /> <br /> You'll note that I said they were the outsider, and I think their design and write-up(s) gets that across wonderfully - if you're going to have an outsider, a weird one, in a collection of freaks and monsters and devils, then making that so by having them interact with a spirit-realm that would make a schizophrenic stop and go &quot;hold up,&quot; is excellent.<br /> They're not &quot;The Other,&quot; though. That's Pandorans and Qashmallim. Riven are strictly the outsider - they get to funk around in two worlds!<br /> They still get the short end of the stick.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S8EuNtxeJKwq4sKVVPe16_N0ylIashKpgfCCuA1UOM8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Promethean Homebrew.</a><br /> <br /> Yes, I made it the same way as a Promethean. No, the authorities haven't found me yet.","edited":{"userid":685,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","user":"Ben Quo","date":". 12-10-2013, 03:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","name":"Ben Quo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar685_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T13:38:49-08:00","id":27482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/14953-ephemeral-lineages?p=27204#post27204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aether/quintessence has been a part of alchemical lore since medieval times.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right; and back when all ephemera were of the same type, that was a somewhat decent justification for them \u2014 although the spirit-orientation still felt odd. It worked back then (to the extent that it did) <i>because</i> all ephemera were made of the same stuff, and because spirits were pretty much anything ephemeral that wasn\u2019t a ghost \u2014 excepting the <i>qashmallim</i>. In many ways, Pyros does a better job of representing the Fifth Element of \u00c6ther as it was conceived by alchemists than ectoplasm does.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/14953-ephemeral-lineages?p=27204#post27204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;The body must still be that of one who had an affinity for spirits: the descendent of shamans, someone with red hair and the Second Sight, one born with the signs of witch-folk or someone who was particularly devout. Those who have experienced interaction with spirits are also likely candidates.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes; that\u2019s what <b>Promethean</b> says about Ulgans; and I have no problem with there being Lineages based on that concept.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/14953-ephemeral-lineages?p=27204#post27204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;It was noted that there was very little presence of quintessence within the terrestrial sphere. Due to the low presence of quintessence, earth could be affected by what takes place within the heavenly bodies.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Thus the tie between alchemy and astrology.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/14953-ephemeral-lineages?p=27204#post27204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;That which is Below corresponds to that which is Above, and that which is Above corresponds to that which is Below, to accomplish the miracle of the One Thing.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Spirits don\u2019t really strike me as being in an \u201cAbove/Below\u201d relationship with the material world without squinting and looking at it sideways \u2014 in other words, shoehorning them into the role for lack of anything better suited. They\u2019re not a <i>bad</i> fit; and they\u2019re a marginally better fit than ghosts; but only marginally so, and they don\u2019t even have that much of an edge compared to, say, angels or astral entities. I don\u2019t see why they should be singled out as <i>the</i> otherworldly entities that Quintessence-based Prometheans should be attuned to.<br /> <br /> Remember, I\u2019m not proposing changing Ulgans; they\u2019re fine as is. I\u2019m proposing adding new Lineages that are similar to Ulgans, but with different foci.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/14953-ephemeral-lineages?p=27204#post27204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Lineage that is elementally infused with the stuff that binds the cosmos together has an affinity for spotting connections that might otherwise be overlooked and is made with the bodies of people who have ties with the supernatural elements of the world that are connected to earthly affairs.</div> </div> </div> </div>And the only disagreement we have here is that you\u2019re saying that this ought to be a singular Lineage, whereas I see no reason why it shouldn\u2019t be a plurality.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/14953-ephemeral-lineages?p=27204#post27204\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right. They're instead sequestered off in their own arbitrary category like the Hazmat Lineages were. I didn't especially like the Hazmat Lineages. They felt shallow.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you have an issue with the HazMat Lineages, please take it up in the topic devoted to discussing them; this topic isn\u2019t about them<sup>*</sup>. Getting back to the main point, I don\u2019t see what\u2019s so arbitrary about \u201cdifferent kinds of ephemera\u201d, or how introducing Lineages inspired by ghosts, angels, and other ephemeral beings sequesters the Ulgans. To me, that sounds like you\u2019re saying that anything that intrudes on the Ulgans\u2019 current monopoly on dealing with the Other damages the Ulgans.<br /> <hr /><span style=\"font-size:9px\">* Seriously, please do. Though I prefer constructive criticism to wholly negative posts.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 12-10-2013, 04:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T13:44:17-08:00","id":27490,"title":"","content":"Ben: the Nuclear Prometheans were conceived to be the \u201coutsiders among outsiders\u201d, not the Ulgans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T14:16:57-08:00","id":27527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/14953-ephemeral-lineages?p=27490#post27490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ben: the Nuclear Prometheans were conceived to be the \u201coutsiders among outsiders\u201d, not the Ulgans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are you saying my reading is incorrect, or are you saying that they are also outsiders?<br /> For what it's worth, I find the Nuclear Prometheans as optional as the Unfleshed, the Constructed, the non-human Prometheans, et. al. They are a rumor.<br /> Really, I feel like the part of Magnum Opus that always sticks with me is &quot;these alternate Prometheans make players question the nature and result of the Pilgrimage,&quot; and I think you could easily label any of then as &quot;the outsider.&quot;<br /> I don't think it makes the Ulgan any less outsider-y.<br /> <br /> Though I'll cede that the ultimate outsider in Promethean is that without myth, since the five base Lineages all have an origin story rooted in some bit of world mythology (which would, in my mind, be the Zeka). I don't want to mince words with you (since it would be pointless), but I understand what you're saying.<br /> <br /> I still think the Ulgan have a unique stance on the Outsider that the other Lineages don't. I guess that's my point; every Lineage has a unique stance the others don't. If you want to an &quot;outsider among outsiders,&quot; that means you have things &quot;beyond the normal ken&quot; to begin with, and the shaman aspect makes them uniquely weird in a way the others aren't.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/14953-ephemeral-lineages?p=27490#post27490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remember, I\u2019m not proposing changing Ulgans; they\u2019re fine as is. I\u2019m proposing adding new Lineages that are similar to Ulgans, but with different foci.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tangentially, I think the God-Machine Lineage would be a neat adaptation, if you were to run Promethean in the GMC setting with angels and demons and the Principle as diametrically opposed to the G-D M-C-H-N-E.<br /> I still think a ghost lineage would be at-odds with the Osirians, or at least would diminish them. I have wanted a Voudon Lineage for a while, though, and I play with the idea of writing up a Taoist Alchemy one, but hey.<br /> <br /> I'm not really arguing against additional Lineages. I'm arguing against forcing them to be Ephemeral in nature. Requiem already uses &quot;Drauger&quot; as a concept, which is a shame, since that Norse myth basically describes a Promethean. I want that Lineage. I want Mayan sacrifices that came back with a black, smokey foot.<br /> I want evidence of a Lineage that is extinct, fallen with Babylon, peers to the Tammuz but never coming back.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/14953-ephemeral-lineages?p=27490#post27490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the only disagreement we have here is that you\u2019re saying that this ought to be a singular Lineage, whereas I see no reason why it shouldn\u2019t be a plurality.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd rather the plurality be unrelated to something like &quot;Ulgan Spirits, X ghosts, Y angels,&quot; personally.<br /> I'd rather a seemingly organic development, and Osirians dealing with ghosts and Ulgan dealing with spirits and a G-M Lineage involved with angels - that seems more organic then &quot;lets neatly fit the Ulgan in alongside a bunch of Ephermeral Lineages.&quot;<br /> Does that makes sense? The plurality doesn't need to be based in the Ephemeral. It's too neat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1S8EuNtxeJKwq4sKVVPe16_N0ylIashKpgfCCuA1UOM8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Promethean Homebrew.</a><br /> <br /> Yes, I made it the same way as a Promethean. No, the authorities haven't found me yet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/685-ben-quo","name":"Ben Quo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar685_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-10T14:36:57-08:00","id":27538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/14953-ephemeral-lineages?p=27482#post27482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right; and back when all ephemera were of the same type, that was a somewhat decent justification for them \u2014 although the spirit-orientation still felt odd. It worked back then (to the extent that it did) <i>because</i> all ephemera were made of the same stuff, and because spirits were pretty much anything ephemeral that wasn\u2019t a ghost \u2014 excepting the <i>qashmallim</i>. In many ways, Pyros does a better job of representing the Fifth Element of \u00c6ther as it was conceived by alchemists than ectoplasm does.</div> </div> </div> </div>As far back as Werewolf Core one needed different equipment to interact with ghosts than with spirits, a concept that carried over in Mage Core and Changeling Core both, with Promethean being the sole hiccup along the way that nevertheless didn't posit much in terms of interaction between ghosts and spirits as a whole.<br /> <br /> What I'm saying here is that &quot;all ephemera were the same type&quot; was never actually true. Ectoplasm is not ephemera of any type, either, being instead a byproduct of interaction between the mundane world and certain manifestations of ephemera.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Spirits don\u2019t really strike me as being in an \u201cAbove/Below\u201d relationship with the material world without squinting and looking at it sideways \u2014 in other words, shoehorning them into the role for lack of anything better suited.<br /> <br /> They\u2019re not a <i>bad</i> fit; and they\u2019re a marginally better fit than ghosts; but only marginally so, and they don\u2019t even have that much of an edge compared to, say, angels or astral entities. I don\u2019t see why they should be singled out as <i>the</i> otherworldly entities that Quintessence-based Prometheans should be attuned to. </div> </div> </div>They're the ephemeral being that has the most concrete ties to &quot;big picture&quot; cosmology while still being closely tied to the mundane world, up to and including the astrological planets.<br /> <br /> Ghosts are tied up with purely human concerns or locked up in the Underworld, Astral entities <i>can't manifest</i>, the amkhata aren't much more involved than ghosts are on account of their being essentially Pandorans with more inanimate targets, chthonians are among the most alien beings in the World of Darkness, and angels and the qashmallim run up and down the ladder of cosmological scale but nevertheless are more concerned with a divine or pseudodivine Plan than being understandable pre-hindsight.<br /> <br /> Spirits, at least, are concerned with the living world, exist in a context of holding up a cosmological mirror to conventional reality, and can offer a greater variety of agendas \u2014 even outside the Shadow \u2014 that can prompt an Ulgan to do Weird Things to deal with them that underline the challenges the Riven face in their Pilgrimages.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Remember, I\u2019m not proposing changing Ulgans; they\u2019re fine as is. I\u2019m proposing adding new Lineages that are similar to Ulgans, but with different foci. </div> </div> </div>It would rather by necessity have to involve changing Ulgans, since otherwise the Riven encompass most other ephemeral Lineage roles in practical terms.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And the only disagreement we have here is that you\u2019re saying that this ought to be a singular Lineage, whereas I see no reason why it shouldn\u2019t be a plurality. </div> </div> </div>If you want to read &quot;place this two-floor-plus-basement family home that's been furnished with conversation pieces and a number of interesting pets in the same category as a couple of small apartments, each with a box of items labeled with the name of a different type of ephemeral being&quot; as &quot;making a singular into part of a plural,&quot; that is certainly your prerogative, but it is not my argument.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you have an issue with the HazMat Lineages, please take it up in the topic devoted to discussing them; this topic isn\u2019t about them<sup>*</sup>. </div> </div> </div>My issue with them is the same as my issue with sectioning off the Ulgan into a box of Ephemeral Lineages; confusing my drawing a parallel in explaining why I don't like either with a desire to critique a thing which I have not bothered with in the years since its initial presentation is not helpful to discussion of either.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Getting back to the main point, I don\u2019t see what\u2019s so arbitrary about \u201cdifferent kinds of ephemera\u201d, or how introducing Lineages inspired by ghosts, angels, and other ephemeral beings sequesters the Ulgans. To me, that sounds like you\u2019re saying that anything that intrudes on the Ulgans\u2019 current monopoly on dealing with the Other damages the Ulgans. </div> </div> </div>Hoo, boy.<br /> <br /> There is ostensibly a place for me to talk about the similarities between the Shadow and the Hedge or Tartarus and Arcadia, or how the storytelling advice for Underworld ghosts aligns with the symptoms of talecrafting addiction and virtually identical language is used in the Book of Spirits and Geist Core in describing their respective ephemeral beings' being highly desirous creatures, or how the idigam's species-wide singularity aligns in description with the wording used to describe the uniqueness of the Extempore, or the way that the interval for a body's viable freshness for both the generative act and the post-mortem Embrace is the same, or any number of other things in the giant pile of strings and clippings I've accumulated over the years.<br /> <br /> This place is not that place, though, so I'll just keep it brief and point out that when a Lineage is aspected toward &quot;the visible light spectrum,&quot; it looks a bit goofy to push for Lineages aspected toward &quot;warm colors&quot; and &quot;cool colors&quot; with no especial concern for the deeper roots of those elements and what they bring to the table beyond &quot;they are more specific bands of color.&quot; The cosmology is not so neatly divided as all that, and motions to the effect that it ought to be consequently tend to ring shallow to me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 12-10-2013, 05:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-15T00:06:30-08:00","id":30313,"title":"","content":"How do I put this? <br /> <br /> Before GMC, ghosts and spirits were the \u201csame type of being\u201d in that they were made of the same ephemeral stuff, and thus could see and touch each other while in Twilight. I never claimed that they were interchangeable with each other, and have myself pointed out how the ghost/spirit divide is as old as ghosts and spirits coexisting in the setting (though I usually point to <b>Second Sight</b> for supporting evidence). <br /> <br /> Yes, the Ulgans are far more developed than the other \u201cEphemeral Lineages\u201d. This is to be expected, because Ulgans have been thoroughly developed by professional game designers whereas the other Ephemeral Lineages are being developed by amateur fans. Sometimes amateurs produce professional-quality work; but that\u2019s the exception rather than the rule. And it\u2019s <i>certainly</i> not to be expected when the development is in the brainstorming stage. <br /> <br /> As for the light spectrum analogy: to me, it isn\u2019t about \u201cvisible light\u201d Ulgans vs. \u201cwarm colors\u201d and \u201ccool colors\u201d; it\u2019s about visible light vs. infrared, ultraviolet, and x-rays: there\u2019s a bit of overlap on the fringes, but that\u2019s about it. Everything about how the Ulgans are written focuses primarily on <i>spirits</i> \u2014 the denizens of the Shadow who were first introduced in <b>Werewolf</b>. Could the Ulgans be <i>rewritten</i> to have a broader scope and to be the one and only Lineage that deals with every kind of ephemeral being equally (in the analogy, could they be broadened from visible light to encompass the entire electromagnetic spectrum)? Sure; but that <i>would</i> be a rewrite, and one that would largely water them down by trying to make them cover too many distinct things that only have an ephemeral state of being in common: ghosts, spirits, angels, and demons share very little in common with each other thematically, something that you pointed out at the start of your post. <br /> <br /> If you don\u2019t like the direction I\u2019m discussing here, so be it \u2014 reasonable people can disagree. But what I\u2019m hearing from you isn\u2019t that it isn\u2019t your cup of tea; what I\u2019m hearing is a declaration that no reasonable person could like the idea. If I read too much into your claims, I apologize; but frankly, I\u2019m getting a distinct sense of being attacked for presuming to even suggest such a thing. In short, there\u2019s no constructive criticism; just \u201cabandon all hope, ye who enter here\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-16T06:39:31-08:00","id":30937,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Satchel:</b><br /> Aether/quintessence has been a part of alchemical lore since medieval times. </div> </div> </div>Though it originally meant something more like pure energy than spirit/ectoplasm; spirits partook of all the elements.<br /> <br /> (That nitpick aside, I find myself wondering what an energy Lineage would be like).<br /> <br /> It also reminds me of another point. While these days, metal is assumed to be a subset of earth, back then it was considered to be a good balance of all the four/five elements (gold of course being the perfect balance). Might that mean that some consider the Unfleshed to be, paradoxically, closer to Elpis and this Mortality than regular Prometheans?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Dataweaver:</b><br /> They\u2019re not a bad fit; and they\u2019re a marginally better fit than ghosts; but only marginally so, and they don\u2019t even have that much of an edge compared to, say, angels or astral entities. I don\u2019t see why they should be singled out as the otherworldly entities that Quintessence-based Prometheans should be attuned to. </div> </div> </div>&quot;Airy spirits&quot; would be the logical fit, and the spirits of the Hisil are the closest thing the NWoD has without inventing something new, which would be overkill for one Promethean lineage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Ben Quo:</b><br /> I'd rather the plurality be unrelated to something like &quot;Ulgan Spirits, X ghosts, Y angels,&quot; personally. </div> </div> </div>That's one reason I suggested having ephemeral Lineages also based off of the big four elements, and have the kind of spirit they associate with be sort of coincidental to that.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-19T00:59:34-08:00","id":33003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/14953-ephemeral-lineages?p=30937#post30937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Airy spirits&quot; would be the logical fit, and the spirits of the Hisil are the closest thing the NWoD has without inventing something new, which would be overkill for one Promethean lineage.</div> </div> </div> </div>For good measure, <a href=\"http://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spirit#Etymology\" target=\"_blank\">the etymology lines up.</a><br /> <br /> Insofar as I've given consideration to the notion of dividing ephemeral beings into association with different Lineages I'd be more inclined to follow the model suggested by Nepri-as-ghost-Lineage and spread the Ulgans out accordingly \u2014 the Golems fit decently into the associations angels and the God-Machine work with, and it's not much work to tie the Galateids to Bacchanalia and other ecstatic behavior and stick the Frankensteins with the qashmallim.*<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:11px\">* Though technically speaking there's thematic elements present in the latter two that fit well enough with the God-Machine \u2014 the Muses' mannequinesque traits, the Wretched's secondary Bestowment \u2014 I feel as though the melancholic humor's sense of easy resignation, the static nature of their Bestowments, and the chthonic imagery of their Wasteland (sinkholes, anyone?) all tie in better.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}